  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="bc460aee-42d6-561a-986b-c5474c4d6a36" activityNameId="60a6ebf8-0a55-581f-b046-4077c5979928" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Polyvinylbutyral, powder, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Polyvinylbutyral, powder, at plant
Material inputs are based on industrial data. Other inventory data are based on rough estimations.;
CAS number: 63148-65-2; 
Synonyms: Mowital B, Pioloform B, Butvar, Rhonival B, S-lec, Vinylite; 
UUID: 0ad77f60-9e4c-3466-b997-54b17b75daca
Included are raw materials and chemicals used for production, transport of materials to manufacturing plant, estimated emissions to air and water from production (incomplete), estimation of energy demand and infrastructure of the plant (approximation). Solid wastes omitted.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The synthesis of PVB starts from polyvinyl alcohol (acetalization). The acetalization is carried out either in water or in alcohols (methanol or ethanol) and is catalyzed with acids (sulfuric or hydrochloric acid). After the reaction the PVB is obtained as a precipitate. Filtering and washing steps as well as final drying are typically carried out after the chemical reaction.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: World production of PVB in 1990 was 80'000t
Sampling: Literature and industry data. 
Extrapolations: Generic data for energy consumption are applied.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0ad77f60-9e4c-3466-b997-54b17b75daca.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: &lt;null&gt;</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: The synthesis of PVB starts from polyvinyl alcohol (acetalization). The acetalization is carried out either in water or in alcohols (methanol or ethanol) and is catalyzed with acids (sulfuric or hydrochloric acid). After the reaction the PVB is obtained as a precipitate. Filtering and washing steps as well as final drying are typically carried out after the chemical reaction.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
      <timePeriod startDate="2007-01-01" endDate="2009-12-31" isDataValidForEntirePeriod="true">
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Time period: Time of publications.</text>
        </comment>
      </timePeriod>
